1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,280
It happens in silence. One day, the kindest person you know simply disappears from your life.

2
00:00:05,480 --> 00:00:09,380
No warning, no explanation, no final conversation. They're just gone.

3
00:00:09,960 --> 00:00:12,620
And according to Carl Jung, this is not coldness.

4
00:00:12,940 --> 00:00:15,860
This is psychology's most powerful act of becoming.

5
00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:19,300
When someone finally cuts everyone off, they aren't losing themselves.

6
00:00:19,420 --> 00:00:20,760
They're returning to themselves.

7
00:00:21,460 --> 00:00:24,520
And once that process begins, nothing reverses it.

8
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:28,820
Jung spent decades studying this pattern, and what he found surprised everyone.

9
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:32,140
These weren't the difficult people. These weren't the ones holding grudges.

10
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:35,620
These were the ones who stayed the longest, who forgave the most,

11
00:00:36,020 --> 00:00:40,960
who absorbed what others couldn't, and kept showing up anyway, until the day they didn't.

12
00:00:41,640 --> 00:00:45,240
And Jung didn't call that a collapse. He called it an awakening.

13
00:00:46,060 --> 00:00:48,840
Here's what most people never understand about the person who walked away.

14
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:50,980
They didn't decide this recently.

15
00:00:51,640 --> 00:00:56,080
The decision was made quietly over years, and Jung called it the accumulation phase.

16
00:00:56,080 --> 00:01:01,300
The long, silent period where the unconscious mind is keeping a record of the conscious mind,

17
00:01:01,840 --> 00:01:03,280
refuses to acknowledge.

18
00:01:04,240 --> 00:01:08,020
Every time their generosity was treated as obligation, recorded.

19
00:01:08,360 --> 00:01:11,640
Every time their patient was mistaken for permission, recorded.

20
00:01:12,020 --> 00:01:15,220
Every time they swallowed something that deserved to be said, recorded.

21
00:01:15,760 --> 00:01:17,980
They never mentioned it. They never showed it.

22
00:01:18,380 --> 00:01:22,420
They kept giving, kept forgiving, kept making themselves available to people

23
00:01:22,420 --> 00:01:25,100
who had stopped making themselves worthy of it.

24
00:01:25,700 --> 00:01:27,280
But something deeper was counting.

25
00:01:27,620 --> 00:01:30,240
And kind people, truly kind people, are not weak.

26
00:01:30,720 --> 00:01:31,540
They are precise.

27
00:01:32,220 --> 00:01:35,080
This is where Jung's concept of the shadow becomes everything.

28
00:01:35,840 --> 00:01:36,960
Everyone carries a shadow.

29
00:01:37,480 --> 00:01:39,400
The unacknowledged parts of the self.

30
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:42,220
For most people, it holds the darker impulses.

31
00:01:42,380 --> 00:01:44,400
The anger they won't admit to.

32
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:46,720
The selfishness they pretend isn't there.

33
00:01:46,720 --> 00:01:51,400
But for the chronic giver, the one who learned early that their needs were inconvenient,

34
00:01:52,160 --> 00:01:54,520
the shadow holds something else entirely.

35
00:01:55,080 --> 00:01:58,880
Their strength, their boundaries, their capacity to choose themselves,

36
00:01:59,380 --> 00:02:03,580
their ability to walk away from what was never truly reciprocated.

37
00:02:04,340 --> 00:02:07,540
And when that shadow finally activates, it doesn't explain itself.

38
00:02:07,900 --> 00:02:09,120
It doesn't offer closure.

39
00:02:09,860 --> 00:02:12,600
It doesn't wait for the right moment or the right words or the right understanding

40
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:14,800
from people who never tried to understand them before.

41
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:19,300
It simply moves completely, finally, without looking back.

42
00:02:20,320 --> 00:02:21,640
And this is called individuation.

43
00:02:22,160 --> 00:02:23,960
The process of becoming fully yourself.

44
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:26,560
Not the version of yourself built around everyone else's comfort.

45
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:28,140
The actual self.

46
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:32,980
The one that exists when the performance of selfishness is finally allowed to end.

47
00:02:33,740 --> 00:02:37,360
And you cannot reach that self while pouring everything you have into people

48
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:40,880
who never once asked if you had enough left for yourself.

49
00:02:41,440 --> 00:02:42,820
The cutting off isn't the loss.

50
00:02:42,820 --> 00:02:45,020
The cutting off is the arrival.

51
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:47,700
The silence you left behind is not emptiness.

52
00:02:48,180 --> 00:02:50,500
It's the sound of a person who gave everything to everyone,

53
00:02:50,660 --> 00:02:52,100
finally giving something to themselves.

54
00:02:52,100 --> 00:02:57,500
So let's talk to you about the more learned and more information.

55
00:02:57,500 --> 00:02:58,660
Thank you.

56
00:02:58,800 --> 00:02:59,200
Yeah.

